.TH DURATION 1 "2026-05-12" "duration" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
duration \- calculate total duration of video or audio files

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B duration
[\fIoptions\fR] <files|directories>

.SH DESCRIPTION
duration is a command-line tool that calculates total duration of media files.

It supports video and audio formats and scans directories recursively.

Unlike older versions, it uses ffmpeg libraries directly (libavformat), not external ffprobe processes.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -v
calculate video duration (default mode)

.TP
.B -a
calculate audio duration

.TP
.B --all
scan directories recursively

.TP
.B -l
list duration of each file in addition to total

.TP
.B -h, --help
show help message

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
duration
scan current directory (video mode)

.TP
duration --all videos/
recursively scan video files

.TP
duration -a music/
scan audio files in folder

.TP
duration -l --all videos/
list each file duration + total

.SH NOTES
This tool uses ffmpeg libraries (libavformat, libavutil).
No external ffprobe process is used.

